{
  "body_human_readable": "## Tesla's 2024 Full-Year Car Sales Reach Nearly 1.8 Million Vehicles\n\nIn a year marked by increased competition and shifting market dynamics, Tesla reported total global vehicle deliveries of approximately 1.79 million for the full year of 2024. The more precise figure stands at 1,789,226 vehicles delivered. This represents a slight decrease of about 1% from the 1.81 million vehicles sold in 2023, marking the company's first annual sales drop in over a decade.\n\nThe vast majority of these sales were driven by the continued popularity of the Model 3 and Model Y, which together accounted for 1,704,093 units. The remaining 85,133 deliveries consisted of the higher-end Model S and Model X, as well as the newly introduced Cybertruck.\n\nDespite the slight annual decline, Tesla's fourth-quarter performance showed a 2.3% increase in sales, with 495,570 vehicles delivered from October through December. This late-year push was supported by incentives such as 0% financing and free charging.\n\nGlobally, Tesla maintained its position as a top seller in the electric vehicle market, narrowly outselling its rival BYD in all-electric vehicle sales. While BYD saw a significant surge in overall vehicle sales, which include plug-in hybrids, Tesla's focus remains solely on battery-electric vehicles. The Model Y continued to be a best-seller in several European countries in 2024.",
